ons or inner lists. Assess only source code visible in the file.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"test_solution.py contains at least two unittest test methods that exercise the public API, covering ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read test_solution.py. Determine whether it uses standard-library unittest, defines at least two test methods, and exercises the public flatten API with ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs. Assess only test content visible in the file; do not infer execution results.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The requested unittest discovery command completes successfully.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative to the supplied task workspace; solution.py and test_solution.py may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"Assume the public function is named flatten and is defined in solution.py, as implied by the request.\\\",\\\"Assume unittest discovery from the workspace root discovers test_solution.py and its test methods.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17389,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":578,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
